+# Conflicting descriptions, copy classes and deferred inputs
+
+October 30, 2026. This source unit supplements the existing PD01–PD07 queue; it does not replace it or a shared master register.
+
+## Preserve each observation in its own role
+
+| Record A | Record B | Relationship and unresolved issue |
+|---|---|---|
+| N1-237-05-004 item 1(a): permanent originals/audio re-recordings | Item 1(b): website-image backups, 60 days after specified cutoff | Different source-defined classes. Do not apply a copy trigger to an unidentified original. Actual membership, website removal, designation and disposition are unverified. |
+| Item 2(a): 180 days after producing recordkeeping copy | Item 2(b): completion of dissemination/revision/updating | Different classes and events; neither is the 60-day website-image trigger. Actual recordkeeping-copy content/location and task completion remain unknown. |
+| Special 9/11 consolidation, item 8020.5 | Historical 2970(1)/(2) OIG audit reply/follow-up and 3770(2) action-file routes | Do not choose a governing category without the case-specific classification and historical policy/hold crosswalk. They do not by themselves contradict each other. |
+| Cover says one attached page | Two content/continuation pages follow the cover in the acquired three-page PDF | Low-strength assembly observation. Explanation and exact originally submitted packet are untested. Repeated job labels are context, not authentication of original assembly. |
+| Held parent-series catalog description: 2001–2004 / UD-10D-1 | Schedule cover and certification: 2005; later investigation/correction trail: 2006 | Different dates describe different things. No temporal contradiction or automatic scope inclusion is inferred. Need the accession/series-to-schedule join and records list. |
+
+Source URLs, fingerprints and exact page/item/line locators: [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). No account is silently made controlling; all earlier published findings and their uncertainty remain intact.
+
+## Priority TODOs and acceptance evidence
+
+1. **PD04/PD05 — classification and transfer join.** Obtain the accession/transfer and folder/item lists that explicitly name N1-237-05-004 (or the applicable successor) and identify permanent originals/audio re-recordings. Compare actual record IDs, office provenance, received dates and inclusion/exclusions with series 7419198. Accept a documentary join, not matching titles alone. Route: FAA records-management/System Operations records and NARA RG237 custodial descriptions, without assuming current custody from the 2005 cover.
+2. **PD01 — correction and delivery.** Obtain the corrected May 22, 2003 QFR answer, version/approval trail, attachments, transmission and recipient acknowledgment, including a successor recipient where relevant. Establish whether the actual record was classified in this 9/11 collection or elsewhere. A catalog description is not the corrected answer. Completion requires the substantive answer plus a verifiable delivery chain.
+3. **PD02/PD03 — decision versus implementation.** Obtain signed consideration/action/no-action record, reasons and dates, and the distinct recommendation-response/status/implementation/closure history for CC-2006-085 / 042R0122001. Do not infer no action from a missing public decision. Preserve all report recommendations separately. Route: applicable FAA and DOT OIG program records; personnel material stays subject to its own privacy/access limits.
+4. **PD04/PD05 — governing versions, holds and actual events.** Obtain the classification/records plan, schedule supersession history, applicable investigation-follow-up policy, retention holds, transfer receipts and any actual destruction/disposition authorization for each identified record. A cancelled FAA handbook listing does not alone cancel this NARA schedule. No current-law or historical-compliance conclusion until those inputs are tested.
+5. **PD05 — original/copy completeness.** For any temporary copy, identify its designated recordkeeping original and verify retained attachments, metadata, redactions and version coverage; for audio distinguish original master, re-recording, channels and clock references. Transfer lists and actual retained data are required. Model/decoder/clock testing remains with the technical owner; no duplicate tests claimed here.
+6. **PD04 low-priority provenance — cover date/count.** A clearer official/certified cover or original submission/continuation record could resolve the exact approval day and attachment-count relationship if needed. Preserve current scan and uncertain transcription first. Do not treat inability to read a day or the one-versus-two count as evidence of alteration.
+
+Every item remains deferred until a concrete new source, a directly exposed public record, a supplied local original or a newly available authorized repository permits the test. Missing inputs are TODOs, not evidence that records never existed or were suppressed. This pass does not submit a request, spend fees or contact custodians. It closes none of the eighteen original-record acceptance criteria.
+
+## Untested explanations and what would discriminate
+
+- Ordinary distinction between permanent records and redundant copies: supported as a distinction in the schedule, but actual compliance requires record inventories, copy designations and transfer/disposition receipts.
+- Incomplete or improper preservation of an identified original: not established. Would require the actual applicable class/hold and an evidentiary custody/disposition chain inconsistent with it, with contrary records retained.
+- Another schedule governs a later correction/action file: unresolved. Obtain case classification and applicable policy, rather than infer from dates or generic similarity.
+- Cover/continuation count reflects form preparation or packet assembly: untested. Original submission/continuation documentation would distinguish possibilities. No hypothesis is elevated into an explanation of the present bytes.
