+# FAA September 11 records: permanent originals and temporary copy classes
+
+Research date: October 30, 2026. Follow-up to B129 / PD04–PD05. This is a dated source study, not a replacement master list, a current legal opinion, or a finding of actual destruction.
+
+## What the original schedule adds
+
+**An acquired, three-page NARA-hosted FAA schedule distinguishes permanent originals and audio re-recordings from several temporary copy classes.** The distinction supplies a concrete classification and custody question for missing records. It does not show that a particular corrected answer, investigative file or recording was included, transferred, destroyed, or retained.
+
+[Original SF115: N1-237-05-004](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/n1-237-05-004_sf115.pdf). Response acquired October 30, 2026 at 13:22:13 UTC: HTTP 200, application/pdf, **127,434 bytes**, SHA-256 **121e24707b1bf8ae6c519cacaa7504b89fd78d97b81f0d1a8d44cb075ce0278a**. All three rendered pages were visually read. The fingerprint identifies the acquired bytes; it does not authenticate original authorship or establish the complete historical file.
+
+The exact PDF had appeared in an earlier search log. This pass adds acquisition and page-by-page inspection, not a newly discovered search result. Source scans, full extracted text, signatures and staff/contact information remain outside this public bundle.
+
+## Source findings and limits
+
+### 1. A particular collection and office, not every FAA record
+
+The cover identifies DOT / FAA, **Air Traffic Organization System Operations Services**, with **System Operations Litigation** as the minor subdivision. The scanned job number is N1-237-05-4; the official URL zero-pads the last component as 004. Page 2 item 1, also labeled item 8020.5, describes a consolidation of documents relating to September 11, the four flights, and subsequent federal actions, gathered from headquarters and regional air traffic control facilities. Its non-exhaustive synopsis includes correspondence, email printouts, memoranda, reports, radar/computer data, voice recordings and re-recordings. [Cover and item 1](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/n1-237-05-004_sf115.pdf#page=2), pins S01–S02.
+
+The schedule's description of a full consolidation is preserved as the agency's description. This review has not verified completeness, accession contents, actual record transfers, or inclusion of later CC-2006-085 correction and administrative-action records. The named office is a source-grounded custody lead, not a verified 2006 custodian for every missing file. DOT OIG's own files need their own classification and custody evidence.
+
+### 2. Four classes with different instructions
+
+| Source class | Recorded disposition and trigger | What it does not establish |
+|---|---|---|
+| Page 2, item 1(a): original records and audio re-recordings | Permanent; transfer to NARA | An actual transfer; a complete master recording; every channel, decoder definition or clock reference; equivalence between an original tape and a re-recording. |
+| Page 2, item 1(b): scanned images maintained by FAA as backup to images posted to its website, including redacted and unredacted copies | Temporary; cut off when the associated website images are removed; delete within **60 days of cutoff** | That the underlying original could be destroyed under this copy instruction, that a website removal occurred, or that a particular missing item was this kind of backup. |
+| Page 2 item 2(a), continued on page 3: convenience/generation copies with no further administrative value after making the recordkeeping copy | Temporary; delete/destroy within **180 days after the recordkeeping copy is produced** | That no recordkeeping copy existed, that it was complete, or that all email was disposable after 180 days. |
+| Page 3 item 2(b): dissemination/revision/updating copies maintained in addition to the recordkeeping copy | Temporary; delete when dissemination, revision or updating is complete | The date that task finished, lawful disposal of another record class, or a particular historical deletion. |
+
+Pins S03–S06 provide exact page/item and local extraction-line locators. These are historical instructions described by the source, not directions to delete anything now. **The 60- and 180-day periods have different starting events and apply to different copies.** They are not competing answers to one universal retention period. The permanent original category must be preserved beside the temporary-copy categories when asking what survived.
+
+### 3. Preserve the previously found audit-file routes separately
+
+The earlier review pinned FAA Order 1350.15C, chapter 5, printed page 95 / PDF page 27, item 2970(1): OIG audit-report and agency-reply files, ten years for closed files if action on recommendations has been completed. Item 2970(2) separately describes audit-follow-up review files and four years after final action on recommendations. [Chapter 5](https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/order/finance/1350-15C/media/chapter5.pdf#page=27), retained pin H01.
+
+Chapter 6, printed page 118 / PDF page 22, item 3770(2), supplies a distinct possible adverse/performance-action file route, with its own exclusions and five-year triggers. It does not establish that any covered action was proposed or taken. [Chapter 6](https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/order/finance/1350-15C/media/chapter6.pdf#page=22), retained pin H02.
+
+These descriptions remain side by side. No source acquired here joins an identified missing record to one category or establishes which historical schedule version, hold or transfer instruction governed it. The generic audit descriptions concern audits; the 9/11 schedule describes a particular collection. Finding the special schedule neither invalidates the earlier routes nor makes it govern a later investigation automatically. [Preserved earlier assessment](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/README.md).
+
+### 4. A held catalog relationship, without a proven transfer join
+
+A preserved October 27 catalog capture for FAA digital record 7597271 exposes parent series [7419198, Open Files Relating to the September 11, 2001 Terrorist Attacks on the United States](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7419198), dated 2001–2004, HMS/MLR UD-10D-1. This is a held catalog representation, not a fresh inspection of the parent contents. Its relationship to the item is a concrete archival lead. **No acquired accession list or parent disposition-authority field links that series to this schedule.** Pin C01.
+
+One web-reader attempt to open that exact parent failed at the tool-access layer. No origin HTTP status, archival withholding decision or authentication requirement was established. A separate browser-runtime attempt failed before navigation. Neither result says anything about historical evidence destruction; the parent/accession join remains a TODO. No guessed IDs or repeated failed routes were used to turn that gap into a finding.
+
+### 5. Small cover/assembly observations retained without an accusation
+
+The cover states **one attached page**, while the acquired PDF contains **two content/continuation pages after the cover**. The comparison is one versus two attachment pages, not one versus three total PDF pages. The continuation pages repeat the job label. These observations do not establish the reason for the count, a missing page, substitution, or invalidity. The agency certification date is read as May 25, 2005; the received field as June 16, 2005. The approval field indicates 2005, but its exact day was not confidently transcribed. An apparent October date is not promoted into an exact approved-on date. Pin S01.
+
+## What can reasonably be inferred
+
+**Moderate confidence:** identifying the actual record category and designated recordkeeping copy is necessary before a missing online copy can tell us much about the original's fate. This schedule provides specific classes and offices with which to test that question. **High confidence in the page-level readings of the class/trigger table**, supported by the preserved scan and full three-page visual review; **unresolved** applicability, supersession, completeness and actual custody/disposition.
+
+The strongest objection to treating this as evidence of concealment is in the schedule itself: it expressly treats originals as permanent, while describing several copies as temporary. That does not prove preservation occurred. Conversely, permission to dispose of a qualified copy does not prove disposal occurred or that the original survived. An improper-disposal hypothesis and ordinary-copy-disposition hypothesis both require actual classification, transfer/hold and disposition records. No intent, coordination, wrongdoing or current compliance finding follows from these pages.
+
+## What remains to be obtained or tested
+
+The signed/versioned corrected QFR and delivery acknowledgment (PD01), signed consideration/action/no-action determination (PD02), and recommendation-response/implementation/closure history (PD03) were **not acquired**. PD04 advances only in identifying an original historical classification source. It remains open until the applicable investigation policy and case-specific classification/custodian/version crosswalk are established. PD05's actual transfer, hold and disposition records remain open too. Recommendations 1–2 and 3–4, investigative closure, recommendation resolution, implementation, correction delivery and personnel action remain distinct outcomes.
+
+[CONFLICTS-AND-TODOS.md](CONFLICTS-AND-TODOS.md) preserves the classes, weak format observation, untested explanations and discriminating inputs. No agency request, mailbox access, fee, private publication or media repopulation was performed. Recorder/materials/clock testing remains with its assigned technical chat. All five original-record work-plan tracks and all eighteen substantive acceptance criteria remain unfinished; publication is not substantive completion.
+
+## Verification and revision record
+
+[SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) records source bytes, dates, item/page/line locators and actual reading scope. Line numbers refer to named local extraction-navigation files, which are not published; original PDF pages/items remain the public verification route. Prior-source pins are reused with their original access dates rather than claimed as new downloads. [REVIEW-CHECKLIST.md](REVIEW-CHECKLIST.md) records scope, checks and exclusions. [REVISION.diff](REVISION.diff) is the exact additive text diff against the absent predecessor path; existing evidence records were not replaced. [MANIFEST.json](MANIFEST.json) fingerprints the five companion files without a recursive self-hash. Public commit/ref and remote verification are reported separately after the actual push.
