+# Review checklist and actual scope
+
+October 30, 2026; source study B129 / PD04–PD05. This is an additive review of one original schedule, with reused historical pins. It is not a new comprehensive audit of every source, a litigation filing, or completion of the original-record goal.
+
+| Required point | Outcome/location | Source verification and remaining limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| Pursue a genuinely available original rather than repeat summaries/searches | README sections 1–2 | Acquired exact previously logged NARA PDF; SHA-256 and byte count rechecked. All three Poppler-rendered pages visually read. |
+| Preserve conflicting records/values and source links | README sections 2–5; CONFLICTS-AND-TODOS | Four copy/original classes, differing triggers, earlier audit/action routes and cover count/date limits remain distinct. No adjudicated category or cause. |
+| Exact locators and provenance | SOURCE-PINS | Official URL, access time, hash, physical PDF page, item and local navigation-line range. Local extraction has OCR errors; visual pages control these transcriptions. |
+| Avoid a classification shortcut | README sections 1, 3–4; TODOs 1, 4 | No actual case-to-schedule or accession/series join acquired. Later investigation/action files not presumed covered. |
+| Missing inputs stay TODOs while useful work continues | CONFLICTS-AND-TODOS | PD01–PD05 targets and acceptance evidence retained. No new original correction, delivery or action/no-action record claimed. |
+| Read/test only actual scope | README scope paragraphs | Three-page schedule read in full; prior chapter 5/6 pins reused, not reread as whole handbooks. Parent relationship from held October27 capture only; live parent access unsuccessful. No technical recorder/materials/clock testing. |
+| Consider disconfirming evidence | README inference section | Permanent originals category limits the inference from temporary-copy rules. Actual compliance is equally unverified. |
+| Keep five tracks/eighteen substantive criteria open | README and TODO final paragraphs | FAA partial source acquisition only; telephone, recorder, materials and steel acceptance work remains separate and unfinished. No percentage of proof. |
+| Preserve sources and previous versions | Native acquisition/notes and this derivative | Native PDF/response/renders retained in verified Intel store; earlier public records unchanged. Nothing deleted, deduplicated or overwritten. |
+| Revision accountability | REVISION.diff | Exact additive diff for the four substantive note/pin/checklist files against no prior file at these unique paths. No existing text changed. |
+| Safe public payload | Six-file manifest | Reviewed original notes, safe selected fields, TODOs, checklist, diff and hashes only. No raw PDF/image/OCR/full source text, signatures, staff/contact data, personal information, case correspondence or strategy. |
+| Publication accountability | Separate actual Git/API receipts after push | Public repository/account/branch/commit metadata, exact staged blobs and remote file bodies must be verified; this checklist does not declare a future push successful. |
+
+## Actual mechanical checks before staging
+
+- Acquired PDF: 127,434 bytes; SHA-256 121e24707b1bf8ae6c519cacaa7504b89fd78d97b81f0d1a8d44cb075ce0278a; three pages; no embedded-attachment names reported by parser.
+- Local page-navigation locator ranges were checked against the held extraction, and class readings against all three rendered pages. The public source remains the scan, not a corrected OCR transcript.
+- JSON parsed; companion-file hashes recomputed; native note copies compared byte-for-byte with the public derivative; exact diff generated from those same bytes.
+- Destination path absent in both inspected branch and fetched main trees before adding. Existing isolated public checkout had an empty index and no unrelated changes at preflight.
+- No software behavior was changed; no experimental replication, policy-applicability, case-custody or legal-compliance test was performed. Structural/hash checks do not validate historical claims.
